# Backup / export restore compatibility

Users rely on restoring backups and exports made with older app builds.

## When proposing or making changes, call out restore risk explicitly if you:

- Bump or tighten `TRANSFER_FORMAT_VERSION`, `ZIP_TRANSFER_FORMAT_VERSION`, or `UPDATE_FORMAT_VERSION` without a migration path for older files
- Change `kind` values (`property-inventory`, `property-update`) or require new top-level fields that `parseTransferBundle` / ZIP import reject
- Change `AppState.version` or make `normalizeState` / `coerceAppState` drop or empty older payloads
- Rename/remove persisted fields without reading legacy keys in `storage.ts` normalize helpers
- Change ZIP layout (`state.json`, `photos/`, `documents/`) or how media ids map to files
- Make import UI or merge/replace logic unable to apply a previously valid package

## Usually safe (no restore-break warning needed):

- New optional fields, arrays defaulting to `[]`, new item types
- UI-only changes, prefs, help text
- Additive normalize/migrate logic that still accepts old shapes

## If a breaking change is intentional

Say so up front, explain what old backups will fail with, and prefer a migration or dual-read over a hard version bump unless the user asks for a break.
